# Exclude Gradle build output from the Docker build context.
# This applies to the IN-CONTAINER BUILDERS (Dockerfile.azure, Dockerfile): without
# it, pre-built JARs from the CI runner are copied into the builder stage and
# Gradle treats them as UP-TO-DATE, skipping processAot entirely. Those builder
# stages must always run a clean Gradle build inside Docker so that processAot
# generates the AOT initializer classes and bootJar bundles them.
# Dockerfile.candidate (the R-C candidate copy-only recipe) does not build
# in-container at all -- it copies a host-verified jar from
# .candidate-artifacts/, which is NOT under build/ and is therefore unaffected by
# this exclusion, same as Dockerfile.slim-it's .slim-it-artifacts/ precedent.
**/build/
**/.gradle/

# Frontend and infrastructure are not needed for backend Docker builds
frontend/
infrastructure/
docs/
logs/
*.md
.git/
.github/
.kiro/
.cursor/
.vscode/
.idea/
.env*
!.env.example
